logs/
# Raw generations stay out; the report artifacts the paper's numbers trace to
# come IN. paper_numbers.json points at results/diag/**, so keeping that
# ignored would mean "every number traces to an artifact" was only true of a
# bundle nobody has seen. A reviewer clones the repo, not the bundle.
results/*
!results/diag/
*.log
*.npy
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.safetensors
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.sync-state
publication_strategy.md
research_landscape.md

.DS_Store
